Instance memory protection tests
================================

The SQL extension checks deterministic pressure state transitions, cgroup and
private-memory parsers, candidate ranking, observer permissions and reload/restart.

Run in a configured build tree:
  make -C src/test/modules/test_memory_protector check

Build and install the test extension into a PRIVATE PostgreSQL installation,
then run the stdlib-only libpq integration suite (no TAP dependencies):
  make -C src/test/modules/test_memory_protector all install
  python3 /absolute/source/path/src/test/modules/test_memory_protector/test_actions.py /absolute/private/install/prefix

This creates a disposable socket-only cluster. It tests observe gating,
simple/extended query cancellation, failed transactions, stale generations and
statements, action expiry, deferred escalation, mode-off revocation, protected
superuser sessions, idle/active termination, and parallel worker protection and
cleanup. Test-only dispatch functions are revoked from PUBLIC; the dispatch
function also checks superuser(). Never install this extension in production.
No test fabricates actual OOM or modifies host cgroups.

macOS/non-Linux reports unsupported_platform. The action suite injects requests
through the test-only dispatcher, so passing it does not certify automatic Linux
pressure selection. Real procfs sampling, cgroup enforcement under load, jemalloc
behavior, and Taurus SAL/IPC cleanup require separate Linux/Taurus acceptance.
The native collector permits enforcement only with a finite local limit and a
visible true hierarchy root with unlimited ancestors. Hidden or constrained
ancestor layouts remain observational. The instance must have a dedicated cgroup.

Parallel private-memory estimates are lower bounds: each round reads at most
eight eligible leaders and eight workers divided fairly among those leaders.
Each leader has a rotating worker cursor. Missing/stale measurements are excluded.

Catalog changes require a new development cluster. Rebuild the extension when
its backend header changes; do not use a stale test extension binary.
